{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q7265454","formula":"C₁₈H₁₄N₂O","hill":"C18H14N2O","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":18.0,"H":14.0,"N":2.0,"O":1.0},"names":{"en":"QH-II-66"},"descriptions":{"en":"QH-II-66 (QH-ii-066) is a sedative drug which is a benzodiazepine derivative. It produces some of the same effects as other benzodiazepines, but is much more selective than most other drugs of this class and so produces somewhat less sedation and ataxia than other related drugs such as diazepam and triazolam, although it still retains anticonvulsant effects. QH-ii-066 is a highly subtype-selective GABAA agonist which was designed to bind selectively to the α5 subtype of GABAA receptors."},"fame":7,"pubchemCid":9838431,"mass":274.3,"charge":0,"smiles":"CN1C(=O)CN=C(C2=C1C=CC(=C2)C#C)C3=CC=CC=C3","inchikey":"FESCSZDQOFYRDR-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"7-ethynyl-1-methyl-5-phenyl-3H-1,4-benzodiazepin-2-one","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"9838431","atoms":35,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":2.35,"y":3.602,"z":0.013,"el":"O"},{"x":2.309,"y":1.335,"z":-0.527,"el":"N"},{"x":-0.172,"y":1.969,"z":1.104,"el":"N"},{"x":0.52,"y":-0.233,"z":0.256,"el":"C"},{"x":1.796,"y":0.012,"z":-0.294,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.465,"y":0.857,"z":0.518,"el":"C"},{"x":1.201,"y":2.172,"z":1.515,"el":"C"},{"x":1.99,"y":2.447,"z":0.26,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.876,"y":0.678,"z":0.07,"el":"C"},{"x":0.099,"y":-1.549,"z":0.52,"el":"C"},{"x":2.584,"y":-1.105,"z":-0.636,"el":"C"},{"x":3.272,"y":1.517,"z":-1.613,"el":"C"},{"x":0.913,"y":-2.631,"z":0.2,"el":"C"},{"x":2.15,"y":-2.409,"z":-0.39,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.147,"y":-0.095,"z":-1.053,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.905,"y":1.286,"z":0.779,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.466,"y":-0.263,"z":-1.473,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.224,"y":1.117,"z":0.359,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.505,"y":0.343,"z":-0.767,"el